                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is an AWESOME game. The level really immerses you into its world. The exploration factor and the fact that there’s hidden secrets all over the world combined with an amazing variety in the weapons you can find to fend off the enemies that come for you. On top of that, the hunger and thirst mechanics really push the survival idea which immerses you further. However, it does have its drawbacks. It’s very unoptimized which makes for some interesting gameplay. The hunger and thirst both drain very fast though which forces you to make a stop in between each progression to eat and drink, along with hopefully healing from the wounds you’ve acquired from the foes in your path. I could not recommend this game more, and it’s my best purchase this year overall.\n\n\nEdit: I'm at 50 hours and man i just gotta say, it really gets good at the 48 hour mark. It's just one of those games that takes some time to learn and once you get the rhythm it's like the pro gamer gameplay really just flows. Well worth a dollar and a play, just gotta be willing to put in the time. If you do, this game is a breeze.",
